WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:02.982
(clicking)

00:00:02.982 --> 00:00:03.815
(rock music)

00:00:03.815 --> 00:00:05.862
- [Narrator] Fear on stage.

00:00:05.862 --> 00:00:08.485
Let's talk stage fright for a second.

00:00:08.485 --> 00:00:09.435
- [Meg Mac] I mean I'm
scared the whole time

00:00:09.435 --> 00:00:11.259
I'm up there in a way.

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:14.761
Most of the time I'm on stage
I just want to be, like, hidden.

00:00:14.761 --> 00:00:17.702
Like, I don't even want
to be visible, you know.

00:00:17.702 --> 00:00:18.535
- [Leon Bridges] You know, I like

00:00:18.535 --> 00:00:20.620
to drink whiskey before I get on stage.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:24.755
If I'm like sober up there I'm
just like awkward and weird.

00:00:24.755 --> 00:00:25.811
- [Halsey] What if I walk
out there and I can't?

00:00:25.811 --> 00:00:26.885
There's a possibility that I can walk

00:00:26.885 --> 00:00:29.289
on that stage and this could suck.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:31.959
I could not sing, I could
freak out, I could panic.

00:00:31.959 --> 00:00:33.992
- [Alt-J] You feel like
you can't trust your body

00:00:33.992 --> 00:00:38.355
to do the most basic movements
that you've grown up doing.

00:00:38.355 --> 00:00:39.343
And it's like vertigo,

00:00:39.343 --> 00:00:42.499
that's how I always describe stage-fright.

00:00:42.499 --> 00:00:45.230
- [Hozier] So at first my throat
used to close up on stage.

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:47.016
You can't really breath
and you can't really sing,

00:00:47.016 --> 00:00:48.781
you know, fuck that you have to do it.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:50.225
You just have to walk through that fire

00:00:50.225 --> 00:00:51.451
and come out the other end.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.284
(static)

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:53.379
- [Narrator] That's exactly what I needed.

00:00:53.379 --> 00:00:54.212
Good.

00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:55.045
(static)

00:00:55.045 --> 00:00:57.545
(light music)

